WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.552
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.822 --> 00:10.740
Something is wrong with the sea?

3
00:11.658 --> 00:15.620
Yes! They're doing land reclamation along the coast now, right?

4
00:15.703 --> 00:18.623
Ever since it started, something has been up with the sea.

5
00:18.706 --> 00:22.627
We're catching fewer fish than before, and digging up fewer clams too.

6
00:22.710 --> 00:24.963
That's because of the reclamation work?

7
00:25.046 --> 00:29.384
They're definitely leaking toxins into the sea, I tell you!

8
00:29.467 --> 00:30.468
At the briefing,

9
00:30.552 --> 00:35.098
they said they tested the soil used in the work and found it to be safe.

10
00:35.181 --> 00:38.685
But I'm sure they're using garbage as landfill!

11
00:38.768 --> 00:39.769
Miss,

12
00:39.853 --> 00:44.566
many people in Konan City make a living through fishing or marine tourism.

13
00:44.649 --> 00:47.026
At this rate, we will all lose our jobs.

14
00:47.944 --> 00:50.572
You are the only person we can rely on.

15
00:50.655 --> 00:52.156
Please help us.

16
00:57.579 --> 01:01.374
We conducted a water quality test after the construction started.

17
01:01.457 --> 01:03.877
However, nothing was detected.

18
01:05.545 --> 01:07.338
There is no connection

19
01:07.422 --> 01:10.008
between the sea acting strange and the land reclamation.

20
01:10.633 --> 01:14.179
We believe there are other causes, such as climate change.

21
01:14.262 --> 01:16.014
I hope you understand.

22
01:16.097 --> 01:19.392
That's a lie. It must be because of that construction!

23
01:19.475 --> 01:23.188
-I'm telling you-- -Could you test it one more time?

24
01:23.271 --> 01:25.899
The water quality may have changed after the last test.

25
01:25.982 --> 01:27.442
It's not impossible.

26
01:27.525 --> 01:29.652
That's right. It's just as she says.

27
01:29.736 --> 01:31.613
Re-testing won't change the results.

28
01:33.907 --> 01:35.533
Hey, look!

29
01:35.617 --> 01:37.243
The sea is huge!

30
01:37.327 --> 01:39.078
It sure is. It's huge.

31
01:39.162 --> 01:40.914
I want to go into the sea!

32
01:41.414 --> 01:43.333
You can, once you get a little bigger.

33
01:43.416 --> 01:45.627
Really? When?

34
01:45.710 --> 01:48.713
When you're as tall as Daddy?

35
01:55.678 --> 01:56.804
Okay.

36
01:57.472 --> 01:59.724
During the environmental lawsuit,

37
01:59.807 --> 02:03.686
these water quality figures were accepted as evidence of pollution by the judge.

38
02:03.770 --> 02:06.189
-Thank you. -Have a seat.

39
02:06.272 --> 02:08.191
Just so you know, this is a special favor!

40
02:08.274 --> 02:11.361
Despite you leaving our firm to go independent.

41
02:11.444 --> 02:13.404
I'm counting on you, sir!

42
02:13.488 --> 02:18.076
You're so smooth, calling me "sir" only at times like this.

43
02:18.159 --> 02:20.662
But are you really going to take this on?

44
02:21.496 --> 02:22.914
Of course.

45
02:22.997 --> 02:24.749
There is no way I can abandon them.

46
02:24.832 --> 02:27.001
Still, that place is…

47
02:27.877 --> 02:29.212
What about it?

48
02:29.295 --> 02:31.631
The urban development of Konan City

49
02:31.714 --> 02:35.218
is a pet project of Mr. Furuse, the Minister of MLIT, right?

50
02:35.301 --> 02:38.513
If you try suing, who knows what he will do. I would stay away from it!

51
02:39.097 --> 02:41.140
I want to help the people.

52
02:41.766 --> 02:45.937
Imagine you're screaming in distress, and no one comes to help you.

53
02:47.647 --> 02:50.900
When you feel it's going badly, give up right away!

54
02:51.901 --> 02:54.988
Think about your own well-being.

55
02:55.989 --> 02:57.073
Please.

56
02:57.824 --> 02:59.367
Can you please tell Mr. Furuse

57
02:59.450 --> 03:02.912
about Mr. Suzuhara and the others' appeal just one more time?

58
03:02.996 --> 03:05.206
How many times do I have to tell you?

59
03:05.289 --> 03:07.667
If there really is water pollution,

60
03:07.750 --> 03:12.088
it will eventually affect Konan City's urban development too.

61
03:14.674 --> 03:16.634
Enough already.

62
03:19.554 --> 03:22.974
I think you've already realized it too.

63
03:23.975 --> 03:28.479
Those people, they just want compensation or settlement fees.

64
03:28.563 --> 03:30.440
They all just want money.

65
03:31.315 --> 03:33.401
When will you stop believing their lies?

66
03:34.110 --> 03:36.446
They are genuinely in trouble!

67
03:37.113 --> 03:40.283
Are you in it for the money too?

68
03:42.452 --> 03:45.413
Why do you assume Mr. Suzuhara's group is lying?

69
03:45.496 --> 03:48.791
Do you understand how they felt when they asked for my help?

70
03:48.875 --> 03:50.585
It's not about money.

71
03:50.668 --> 03:54.589
I just want to protect their livelihoods.

72
03:55.673 --> 03:59.677
If that's the case, why don't you investigate it yourselves?

73
04:01.346 --> 04:04.265
I think it would be pointless, though.

74
04:06.184 --> 04:10.063
At any rate, your sense of justice is warped.

75
04:12.023 --> 04:14.901
Asking Mr. Furuse to do a water quality test…

76
04:16.235 --> 04:18.071
will be very difficult.

77
04:22.367 --> 04:23.534
The heck.

78
04:25.078 --> 04:27.288
In the end, you're just like them.

79
04:27.789 --> 04:28.748
Let's go.

80
04:49.018 --> 04:52.438
THIS IS SECRETARY NITOU I WOULD LIKE TO MEET YOU DIRECTLY

81
05:21.634 --> 05:25.096
Mr. Furuse, were you unaware of Sendo's wrongdoing?

82
05:25.179 --> 05:29.183
It is shameful to admit, but I was completely unaware.

83
05:29.892 --> 05:32.895
Some say you received slush funds generated from their fraud.

84
05:32.979 --> 05:34.689
How can you say you don't know?

85
05:34.772 --> 05:38.442
Sendo Construction is involved in the Konan City development,

86
05:38.526 --> 05:40.278
so did they give you kickbacks?

87
05:40.361 --> 05:42.029
Regarding Sendo's wrongdoing,

88
05:42.113 --> 05:46.367
I intend to thoroughly investigate the matter myself.

89
05:46.450 --> 05:50.413
So you are saying you didn't collude with or receive slush funds from them?

90
05:50.496 --> 05:53.291
Of course, I did nothing of the sort.

91
05:53.374 --> 05:56.002
He cut them off so masterfully.

92
05:56.752 --> 05:58.588
Look at this.

93
05:59.172 --> 06:03.217
We found this to be embezzlement by some of our company's employees.

94
06:03.843 --> 06:07.305
We did not provide any financial support to Mr. Furuse!

95
06:08.014 --> 06:12.018
Sendo is fully willing to take the fall. They're saying it's their fault!

96
06:12.101 --> 06:15.646
However, the media will probably be in an uproar for a while.

97
06:15.730 --> 06:17.440
With the rival party lobbying too,

98
06:17.523 --> 06:20.193
Furuse might not be able to handle the resort.

99
06:20.276 --> 06:21.360
Then…

100
06:21.444 --> 06:23.946
he won't be able to mess with us for a while, right?

101
06:24.697 --> 06:27.950
Let's use this opening to prove that Ms. Shiramoto is innocent!

102
06:28.034 --> 06:29.243
Right?

103
06:29.327 --> 06:31.954
Ms. Shiramoto definitely didn't do it.

104
06:32.038 --> 06:33.372
Right, Mr. Uramawashi?

105
06:33.456 --> 06:34.498
I don't know.

106
06:34.582 --> 06:37.793
You "don't know"? Do you not care about Ms. Shiramoto?

107
06:37.877 --> 06:39.212
-Ms. Aso. -Huh?

108
06:39.295 --> 06:41.464
-Ms. Aso. -What is it?

109
06:41.547 --> 06:43.466
-Ms. Aso. -What?

110
06:43.549 --> 06:45.051
-Ms. Aso. -Ms. Aso.

111
06:48.179 --> 06:51.849
Mr. Uramawashi was shocked too, you know.

112
06:51.933 --> 06:53.309
Shocked?

113
06:53.392 --> 06:58.439
I mean, he was fidgeting with that thing faster than usual.

114
06:58.522 --> 07:02.777
But knowing Mr. Uramawashi, he must have something in mind.

115
07:02.860 --> 07:04.612
Let's leave him be for a bit…

116
07:04.695 --> 07:06.447
Oh, Ms. Aso?

117
07:06.530 --> 07:07.573
Ms. Aso.

118
07:08.074 --> 07:09.659
JUSTICE'S FORM

119
07:13.371 --> 07:14.956
I killed Nitou.

120
07:19.585 --> 07:21.504
Knock before you come in!

121
07:21.587 --> 07:23.047
We're going to drink.

122
07:26.842 --> 07:30.263
She must have had her reasons. Don't you think so?

123
07:30.888 --> 07:32.765
-Yeah. -I think so too.

124
07:33.766 --> 07:35.059
Are you listening?

125
07:38.354 --> 07:41.399
Did I hit the bullseye? You feel that way too?

126
07:41.482 --> 07:42.525
You haven't.

127
07:42.608 --> 07:43.734
Let's believe in her.

128
07:43.818 --> 07:46.612
I'm sure Ms. Shiramoto understands how much you fought for her.

129
07:46.696 --> 07:50.032
-I did nothing-- -I mean, you became a lawyer for her sake!

130
07:50.116 --> 07:51.409
-I'm telling you-- -Right!

131
07:51.492 --> 07:54.537
If it's to help Ms. Shiramoto, I'll go along with your lies.

132
07:54.620 --> 07:55.705
I don't need you--

133
07:55.788 --> 07:59.166
Please forget what Ms. Shiramoto said, okay?

134
07:59.709 --> 08:02.003
Well then, excuse me!

135
08:02.086 --> 08:03.629
Bye!

136
08:04.255 --> 08:06.090
-Bye! -See you!

137
08:09.885 --> 08:13.222
As I thought, Ms. Aso was hit the hardest by it.

138
08:13.306 --> 08:16.434
I mean, the person she trusted most just admitted to murder.

139
08:16.517 --> 08:19.478
So, what are you plotting?

140
08:19.562 --> 08:22.648
No way you don't have a plan in mind, right?

141
08:32.908 --> 08:34.160
Ms. Aso.

142
08:34.243 --> 08:36.454
Didn't you say you were going straight home?

143
08:37.538 --> 08:38.831
Ms. Aso.

144
08:40.333 --> 08:41.542
You didn't go home?

145
08:42.960 --> 08:44.170
Not yet.

146
08:44.253 --> 08:45.171
Why?

147
08:45.755 --> 08:48.549
I see, so Ms. Shiramoto admitted to it.

148
08:49.675 --> 08:51.761
I think she was lying.

149
08:52.345 --> 08:55.765
But why did she admit to it, after all these years…

150
08:57.058 --> 09:02.188
I wanted to request a retrial someday and prove Ms. Shiramoto's innocence.

151
09:03.022 --> 09:04.190
And yet…

152
09:06.484 --> 09:10.988
Is there anyone who knows what happened back then I could talk to?

153
09:11.072 --> 09:13.449
There is someone, but…

154
09:13.532 --> 09:14.575
But what?

155
09:15.451 --> 09:18.704
Right after the murder, there was an article, right?

156
09:19.747 --> 09:21.165
Article?

157
09:21.248 --> 09:25.670
Even the victims' association that was planning to file a lawsuit got angry,

158
09:25.753 --> 09:28.089
saying Ms. Shiramoto lied to them.

159
09:28.714 --> 09:32.718
Most of them were given money and moved elsewhere.

160
09:32.802 --> 09:34.220
No way…

161
09:34.762 --> 09:38.224
But the representative, Mr. Suzuhara, should still be in Konan City.

162
09:38.307 --> 09:39.975
Where does he live?

163
09:40.059 --> 09:43.896
I'm not sure if he'll talk to you.

164
09:44.480 --> 09:47.108
Even so, I want to meet him.

165
09:47.900 --> 09:48.901
Okay.

166
09:49.944 --> 09:51.904
But before that…

167
09:57.243 --> 09:59.286
Tomorrow might work.

168
09:59.787 --> 10:01.997
Ms. Aso, are you free tomorrow?

169
10:02.665 --> 10:03.749
What?

170
10:08.295 --> 10:10.131
Mr. Moriki, where are we going?

171
10:13.092 --> 10:15.469
What? The library?

172
10:23.769 --> 10:25.980
Oh, there he is.

173
10:26.063 --> 10:26.981
Yes?

174
10:30.067 --> 10:34.530
That should be him. That boy right at the front.

175
10:34.613 --> 10:36.323
Who is that?

176
10:36.407 --> 10:39.535
Taiji Shiramoto. He's probably in middle school now.

177
10:40.077 --> 10:41.954
Shiramoto?

178
10:42.037 --> 10:44.081
He's Ms. Shiramoto's son.

179
10:44.165 --> 10:45.583
What?

180
10:46.500 --> 10:51.297
Ms. Shiramoto is actually a widow, and when that murder happened,

181
10:51.380 --> 10:54.216
her late husband's parents took him in.

182
10:54.842 --> 10:56.385
Is that so?

183
10:56.469 --> 11:00.890
If she makes an enemy of Mr. Furuse, that boy may also be in danger.

184
11:00.973 --> 11:02.308
That's probably what she thinks.

185
11:09.648 --> 11:11.150
-See you. -Bye.

186
11:12.943 --> 11:13.986
Excuse me…

187
11:15.446 --> 11:16.655
Hello.

188
11:19.366 --> 11:20.743
A lawyer?

189
11:23.454 --> 11:26.165
Wait, hold on!

190
11:29.585 --> 11:32.213
HIGASHIHAMA CITY HALL INADA BRANCH OFFICE

191
11:32.296 --> 11:35.925
Does Taiji know about Ms. Shiramoto?

192
11:36.008 --> 11:38.969
No, he was still very young when the incident happened,

193
11:39.053 --> 11:40.679
so he shouldn't know anything.

194
11:41.430 --> 11:45.601
I'm not sure if he even remembers who Ms. Shiramoto is.

195
11:47.478 --> 11:51.065
When that incident happened, so many things changed.

196
11:53.567 --> 11:56.111
This is Mr. Suzuhara's address.

197
11:56.195 --> 11:57.780
Thank you very much.

198
11:57.863 --> 12:02.284
He's not an easy person to deal with. He'll probably chase you away.

199
12:04.161 --> 12:08.082
Mr. Moriki, why do you help Mr. Uramawashi?

200
12:10.459 --> 12:11.752
To tell the truth,

201
12:11.835 --> 12:14.880
I wanted to take on Ms. Shiramoto's defense.

202
12:14.964 --> 12:16.966
She was a dear coworker.

203
12:17.049 --> 12:18.759
But I couldn't do it.

204
12:20.302 --> 12:24.598
If you get cocky and challenge a powerful politician,

205
12:25.432 --> 12:27.017
it will hurt the people around you.

206
12:28.477 --> 12:31.689
You'll cause a lot of trouble for everyone.

207
12:32.565 --> 12:34.567
The firm's director at the time warned me off.

208
12:36.068 --> 12:37.653
I still regret it today.

209
12:39.154 --> 12:43.367
That's why I want to help this time.

210
12:49.123 --> 12:49.999
Go home!

211
12:50.082 --> 12:53.669
Please, just a moment! What happened ten years ago in Konan City?

212
12:53.752 --> 12:56.213
What happened to Ms. Shiramoto? I want to know!

213
12:56.297 --> 12:57.631
I have nothing to tell you.

214
12:57.715 --> 13:00.426
Ms. Shiramoto might be innocent.

215
13:00.509 --> 13:02.469
Mr. Suzuhara, tell me what you know.

216
13:02.553 --> 13:05.472
I told you to get lost! Don't ever come back!

217
13:12.271 --> 13:16.150
Ms. Shiramoto is not someone who acts for money.

218
13:16.233 --> 13:18.193
She fights fiercely for others' sake.

219
13:19.403 --> 13:21.155
I want to believe that.

220
13:21.238 --> 13:25.701
Please tell me what happened ten years ago.

221
13:26.243 --> 13:29.121
I've already forgotten. Please, just leave.

222
13:39.131 --> 13:41.050
-I'll get the car. -Okay.

223
13:41.967 --> 13:43.218
Mr. Katono.

224
13:44.386 --> 13:47.014
You haven't been to our representative's meetings lately.

225
13:47.097 --> 13:48.724
I'm sorry about that.

226
13:48.807 --> 13:49.850
The election is soon.

227
13:49.933 --> 13:53.687
I've been going back to my constituency and greeting support groups.

228
13:53.771 --> 13:57.816
I understand that, but weren't you very enthusiastic about the resort?

229
14:00.736 --> 14:04.323
The media is all over the matter with Sendo, isn't it?

230
14:04.406 --> 14:06.408
I can't afford to get dragged into it.

231
14:06.492 --> 14:09.495
Aren't you an accomplice too?

232
14:09.578 --> 14:12.581
Yes, and I will repay the favor somehow.

233
14:12.665 --> 14:14.541
Please tell Mr. Furuse that.

234
14:14.625 --> 14:16.627
Well then, excuse me.

235
14:19.713 --> 14:22.299
Bringing Mr. Katono back into the fold won't be easy.

236
14:22.383 --> 14:25.135
Younger members are so quick to jump ship.

237
14:25.219 --> 14:27.054
He bit the hand that fed him.

238
14:27.846 --> 14:29.723
I have an idea.

239
14:30.516 --> 14:33.102
Mr. Yamaguchi was in the same class as Mr. Katono.

240
14:33.185 --> 14:35.187
How about we bring him over to our side?

241
14:35.270 --> 14:38.399
If I recall correctly, he's from the rival party, right?

242
14:39.024 --> 14:42.695
If we bring him into our fold, our network of contacts might expand too.

243
14:43.946 --> 14:46.323
Amazing, Murota. You have an eye for opportunities.

244
14:46.407 --> 14:48.492
I will arrange a meeting right away.

245
14:48.575 --> 14:51.620
You should accompany me, Murota.

246
14:51.704 --> 14:54.206
If you establish a connection with him,

247
14:54.289 --> 14:57.668
your foundation as a politician will become rock solid.

248
14:58.877 --> 15:02.006
Isn't it about time you made your move into the political world?

249
15:02.756 --> 15:04.758
Certainly. Thank you very much.

250
15:09.346 --> 15:10.723
Donghyuk. What is it?

251
15:11.432 --> 15:13.475
Our company's delegation will participate

252
15:13.559 --> 15:16.145
in the Japan-Korea Cultural and Economic Forum,

253
15:16.228 --> 15:18.731
taking place next Friday.

254
15:18.814 --> 15:20.524
Next Friday?

255
15:20.607 --> 15:21.442
Yes.

256
15:23.902 --> 15:25.529
Will you be okay?

257
15:26.238 --> 15:27.406
The Sendo scandal…

258
15:28.073 --> 15:29.450
Don't worry about that.

259
15:29.533 --> 15:32.703
If they ask about Sendo, Murota will speak on my behalf.

260
15:32.786 --> 15:35.456
Understood. Please do.

261
15:35.539 --> 15:37.875
I will come over as soon as my meeting ends.

262
15:37.958 --> 15:41.170
Give my regards to Representative Kang.

263
15:41.253 --> 15:42.671
I will. Goodbye.

264
15:57.853 --> 16:01.940
RGC Resorts Representative Kang Jun-ho will be in Japan in one week.

265
16:02.024 --> 16:04.193
Since the resort plan was announced,

266
16:04.276 --> 16:08.530
he'll probably want to see the site in person, not just attend the event.

267
16:08.614 --> 16:10.532
To establish an integrated resort in Japan,

268
16:10.616 --> 16:14.453
you must have a company with casino experience like RGC,

269
16:14.536 --> 16:16.538
or it won't meet the legal standards.

270
16:16.622 --> 16:22.628
That's why Furuse considers Mr. Kang to be an important partner.

271
16:22.711 --> 16:24.797
If RGC can set up a casino in Japan,

272
16:24.880 --> 16:27.257
vast amounts of money will keep flowing in forever.

273
16:27.341 --> 16:28.801
It's a win-win.

274
16:28.884 --> 16:31.678
But isn't Furuse involved in the slush fund scandal now?

275
16:31.762 --> 16:35.974
On top of that, it seems some of his political allies are starting to dump him.

276
16:36.058 --> 16:37.101
Hey, Nakazaki.

277
16:39.269 --> 16:41.772
He probably used all the money he got from Sendo

278
16:41.855 --> 16:45.275
to bribe politicians to support him.

279
16:45.359 --> 16:49.822
To advance the resort plan, he needs as many allies as he can get.

280
16:49.905 --> 16:53.617
However, once the money runs out, they'll dump him.

281
16:53.700 --> 16:58.413
We have to make sure Mr. Kang understands this situation.

282
16:59.164 --> 17:00.249
However…

283
17:01.041 --> 17:02.751
For that,

284
17:05.087 --> 17:07.631
we need a special pillar.

285
17:07.714 --> 17:09.341
A special pillar?

286
17:16.849 --> 17:18.225
Hup.

287
17:19.351 --> 17:20.894
Good morning.

288
17:23.939 --> 17:25.190
I'll help you!

289
17:26.900 --> 17:28.735
I didn't say you could do that!

290
17:28.819 --> 17:31.530
Come on, doing this work all by yourself must be tough.

291
17:32.072 --> 17:33.323
What's your schedule?

292
17:33.407 --> 17:35.617
Their director wants to talk to me at 4 p.m.

293
17:35.701 --> 17:36.910
Understood.

294
17:37.953 --> 17:39.037
What's wrong?

295
17:39.580 --> 17:41.039
Please go on ahead.

296
17:41.123 --> 17:42.291
Very well.

297
17:50.799 --> 17:52.009
What do you want?

298
17:53.427 --> 17:56.930
Did you ask Furuse about what happened ten years ago?

299
17:57.014 --> 17:58.599
There's no need to ask.

300
17:59.099 --> 18:00.350
I believe in him.

301
18:00.434 --> 18:02.895
Something is bothering you, right?

302
18:09.526 --> 18:14.531
Are you scared of realizing your own mistake?

303
18:19.536 --> 18:25.125
If you're lying to yourself, you won't be able to see anything.

304
18:30.005 --> 18:31.840
The liar here is you.

305
18:37.804 --> 18:39.806
BOARD MEETING ROOM

306
18:45.604 --> 18:47.773
MR. FURUSE

307
19:09.002 --> 19:13.590
Your sister will definitely turn you away.

308
19:16.593 --> 19:18.095
I killed Nitou.

309
19:24.226 --> 19:27.062
Ms. Shiramoto definitely didn't do it!

310
19:30.357 --> 19:32.985
SMALL BANQUET HALL

311
19:44.121 --> 19:45.289
It's done.

312
19:49.001 --> 19:53.338
This blueprint leaves no room for lies to escape.

313
19:57.759 --> 20:01.138
Incredible how Mr. Uramawashi found out all this stuff.

314
20:01.221 --> 20:04.141
-Ms. Konno, how about the costumes? -They're done.

315
20:04.224 --> 20:07.019
Maybe I should start attending a language school.

316
20:07.102 --> 20:10.731
No, a translation app is enough for something like this.

317
20:13.233 --> 20:15.235
Ten more boxes to go!

318
20:16.028 --> 20:18.238
Hey. Why do I have to do it too?

319
20:18.322 --> 20:20.240
Mr. Moriki is working me to the bone!

320
20:20.324 --> 20:22.117
It's fine from time to time!

321
20:22.200 --> 20:23.493
Jeez!

322
20:26.413 --> 20:28.332
You're really going so far for this case.

323
20:28.415 --> 20:31.293
To know someone, you must try living their life.

324
20:31.376 --> 20:33.420
Depending on one's environment and position,

325
20:33.503 --> 20:35.047
the form of justice can change.

326
20:35.672 --> 20:39.968
Not justice as written in books, but "the justice inside you," was it?

327
20:40.052 --> 20:42.304
Did you read Ms. Shiramoto's book too?

328
20:42.387 --> 20:43.472
Well, yeah.

329
20:44.765 --> 20:47.434
To thoroughly become the client's ally,

330
20:47.976 --> 20:50.645
it's harder than it sounds.

331
20:50.729 --> 20:54.733
But I'm sure Ms. Shiramoto tried to do it.

332
20:54.816 --> 20:58.695
Ten years ago, she felt the same as Suzuhara's group and fought for them.

333
20:59.821 --> 21:03.700
So now I must do all I can to fight for her too!

334
21:04.743 --> 21:06.870
Come on, we'll never finish at this rate.

335
21:06.953 --> 21:10.457
I know that, but this is surprisingly difficult.

336
21:11.041 --> 21:13.126
All right, this is the last one.

337
21:13.919 --> 21:14.878
Finally all done.

338
21:14.961 --> 21:16.421
Thank you very much.

339
21:19.383 --> 21:21.927
I didn't ask you to do it!

340
21:22.010 --> 21:23.261
I'm sorry.

341
21:32.687 --> 21:33.980
Enough.

342
21:34.064 --> 21:34.898
What?

343
21:35.482 --> 21:36.566
You…

344
21:37.526 --> 21:39.694
are just like that person.

345
21:45.200 --> 21:49.746
I went to meet Mr. Suzuhara, who tried to file a lawsuit ten years ago.

346
21:51.790 --> 21:53.250
Mr. Suzuhara said…

347
21:54.251 --> 21:57.963
I only met that Nitou person twice.

348
21:58.463 --> 22:01.967
At first, he flatly insisted that there was no water pollution.

349
22:02.050 --> 22:03.468
There is no connection

350
22:03.552 --> 22:05.762
between the sea acting strange and the land reclamation.

351
22:06.430 --> 22:09.599
We believe there are other causes, such as climate change.

352
22:09.683 --> 22:11.268
I hope you understand.

353
22:11.351 --> 22:14.688
That's a lie. It must be because of that construction!

354
22:14.771 --> 22:18.275
-I'm telling you-- -Could you test it one more time?

355
22:18.358 --> 22:20.610
The water quality may have changed after the last test.

356
22:21.194 --> 22:22.696
It's not impossible.

357
22:22.779 --> 22:25.157
After that, Ms. Shiramoto investigated

358
22:25.240 --> 22:28.702
the water quality around the reclaimed land on her own.

359
22:30.620 --> 22:33.999
She found water pollution.

360
22:39.880 --> 22:41.131
Look at this.

361
22:41.715 --> 22:43.508
It really was polluted!

362
22:45.010 --> 22:48.305
Why are the documents you submitted different?

363
22:49.222 --> 22:50.432
Well…

364
22:50.932 --> 22:53.435
We intend to submit this data.

365
22:53.518 --> 22:55.854
Please don't! Wait a moment.

366
22:56.354 --> 23:00.984
If Mr. Suzuhara knew about it, why didn't he tell anyone?

367
23:02.152 --> 23:03.403
That's because…

368
23:05.614 --> 23:06.740
I'm sorry.

369
23:08.867 --> 23:11.286
Honestly, I knew I had to say it.

370
23:13.079 --> 23:14.331
But…

371
23:16.374 --> 23:21.213
I thought Ms. Shiramoto lied to us in order to make money, and I got mad,

372
23:23.798 --> 23:24.841
so I also…

373
23:25.717 --> 23:29.054
took the money.

374
23:32.224 --> 23:34.434
If I did something reckless,

375
23:34.517 --> 23:37.771
they could expose the fact that I took money from them, so I…

376
23:38.480 --> 23:39.856
I got scared.

377
23:41.900 --> 23:44.486
Are you saying Mr. Furuse handed over money

378
23:44.569 --> 23:46.613
to buy his silence?

379
23:46.696 --> 23:48.073
I believe so.

380
23:48.156 --> 23:49.783
No, but still,

381
23:49.866 --> 23:52.577
it doesn't prove Ms. Shiramoto didn't kill my father.

382
23:53.620 --> 23:54.454
It doesn't.

383
23:55.163 --> 23:58.500
However, on the day Mr. Nitou passed away…

384
23:58.583 --> 24:01.878
I got a message from Mr. Nitou just now.

385
24:02.379 --> 24:03.838
I WOULD LIKE TO MEET YOU DIRECTLY

386
24:03.922 --> 24:06.466
I'll meet and talk with him again.

387
24:07.634 --> 24:12.264
I'm sure Mr. Nitou will understand. We just need to talk to him.

388
24:13.556 --> 24:16.851
Maybe he'll even fight together with us.

389
24:19.396 --> 24:20.814
Please take a look at this.

390
24:23.066 --> 24:25.193
Mr. Uramawashi was looking into it.

391
24:27.070 --> 24:29.572
Teito Medical University…

392
24:29.656 --> 24:31.283
From back then…

393
24:31.366 --> 24:32.951
DEATH CERTIFICATE (AUTOPSY RESULTS)

394
24:33.034 --> 24:36.579
This is Mr. Nitou's actual death certificate.

395
24:39.958 --> 24:41.668
Between the time of death

396
24:41.751 --> 24:44.879
and the time Ms. Shiramoto went to see Mr. Nitou,

397
24:44.963 --> 24:46.715
there is a huge gap.

398
24:50.844 --> 24:54.389
Why don't we verify what happened ten years ago?

399
24:55.056 --> 24:57.600
I'm sure Mr. Furuse knows the truth.

400
25:00.437 --> 25:01.646
Donghyuk.

401
25:02.981 --> 25:04.024
I…

402
25:04.774 --> 25:06.943
owe a debt of gratitude to Mr. Furuse.

403
25:08.570 --> 25:10.238
No matter what happened,

404
25:11.197 --> 25:14.826
to me, he is like a second father.

405
25:20.040 --> 25:22.083
LAW

406
25:27.922 --> 25:29.424
JUSTICE'S FORM

407
25:36.723 --> 25:38.433
MIYUKI SHIRAMOTO

408
25:39.851 --> 25:41.227
I have a copy too.

409
25:43.188 --> 25:44.230
JUSTICE'S FORM

410
25:47.108 --> 25:48.318
TALKING CORNER

411
25:48.401 --> 25:50.862
This is my bible.

412
25:50.945 --> 25:52.947
Whenever I'm stuck, I read it.

413
25:53.865 --> 25:55.492
But she's a murderer.

414
25:57.327 --> 25:58.578
Who told you that?

415
25:59.287 --> 26:00.830
No one.

416
26:01.498 --> 26:03.541
Nobody would tell me anyway.

417
26:03.625 --> 26:05.335
I searched her name online.

418
26:06.002 --> 26:08.296
I found a photo of my mother at home,

419
26:09.839 --> 26:11.758
and realized it was probably her.

420
26:12.509 --> 26:16.054
She had a fight over some money and killed a man, right?

421
26:16.805 --> 26:18.348
That's not true.

422
26:18.431 --> 26:19.849
What? But…

423
26:19.933 --> 26:22.227
Everything they wrote about her online is a lie.

424
26:23.186 --> 26:25.980
Your mother would never do something like that.

425
26:28.066 --> 26:30.527
She is an amazing lawyer.

426
26:31.069 --> 26:34.072
She cares about what brings happiness to her client

427
26:34.155 --> 26:37.534
and stays their strongest ally until the very end.

428
26:38.034 --> 26:41.329
The way she stands in court is so cool.

429
26:44.916 --> 26:46.209
Right now,

430
26:46.292 --> 26:49.921
I'm investigating to prove your mother is innocent.

431
26:50.547 --> 26:52.715
That's why I came to see you, Taiji.

432
26:53.967 --> 26:55.635
I don't know anything.

433
26:56.261 --> 26:58.304
I know nothing about my mother.

434
26:59.389 --> 27:02.809
But I need your help.

435
27:03.643 --> 27:04.519
My help?

436
27:05.145 --> 27:06.146
Please.

437
27:06.813 --> 27:08.022
Help me.

438
27:12.861 --> 27:14.237
I'm begging you.

439
27:23.079 --> 27:24.038
Sir,

440
27:24.122 --> 27:27.667
it seems Mr. Furuse will be late today.

441
27:27.750 --> 27:30.837
His secretary is holding a conference at Hotel Bellezza Tokyo

442
27:30.920 --> 27:33.506
to discuss the Sendo scandal.

443
27:33.590 --> 27:35.467
Is that so? I understand.

444
27:44.684 --> 27:46.311
I'll set off now.

445
27:55.320 --> 27:56.863
We're departing now.

446
28:00.200 --> 28:01.117
ELECTION STRATEGY MEETING

447
28:01.826 --> 28:03.745
To explain the situation to Mr. Kang,

448
28:03.828 --> 28:07.624
we will have Mr. Shoji, a famous corporate criminal lawyer, accompany us.

449
28:07.707 --> 28:09.167
I see.

450
28:09.250 --> 28:11.377
Mr. Shoji, please do your best.

451
28:11.461 --> 28:12.712
Leave it to me.

452
28:12.795 --> 28:14.130
By the time Mr. Kang is here,

453
28:14.214 --> 28:17.800
I think we can go back to discussing business, as usual.

454
28:17.884 --> 28:19.052
That's reassuring.

455
28:19.135 --> 28:21.054
-I will get going now. -Good.

456
28:23.806 --> 28:25.099
Mr. Kang has arrived.

457
28:25.975 --> 28:27.268
GUEST ENTRANCE

458
28:29.479 --> 28:31.481
This way, please.

459
28:31.564 --> 28:33.691
-Huh? What's going on? -This way, please.

460
28:33.775 --> 28:36.152
Are they parking the car?

461
28:53.753 --> 28:55.463
Welcome.

462
28:55.547 --> 28:58.007
Please follow me.

463
29:04.138 --> 29:05.348
Ms. Konno, let's go.

464
29:06.140 --> 29:07.141
Got it.

465
29:23.992 --> 29:28.454
Mr. Murota, Mr. Shoji, thank you for using our hotel today.

466
29:28.538 --> 29:29.998
Right this way, please.

467
29:45.889 --> 29:47.599
Right this way.

468
30:10.330 --> 30:14.959
You came a long way to get here. I hope your effort wasn't in vain.

469
30:15.043 --> 30:16.419
Representative Kang.

470
30:16.502 --> 30:17.879
Who are you?

471
30:19.005 --> 30:20.548
Long time no see, Mr. Murota.

472
30:20.632 --> 30:21.925
What is the meaning of this?

473
30:22.008 --> 30:23.676
Since Furuse couldn't make it,

474
30:23.760 --> 30:28.222
I thought I would share the recent news from Japan

475
30:29.474 --> 30:30.934
with our representative here.

476
30:31.601 --> 30:32.769
Who is he?

477
30:34.228 --> 30:35.939
Shall we call the police?

478
30:36.022 --> 30:37.607
Please do.

479
30:41.361 --> 30:42.987
Take a look at this.

480
31:04.676 --> 31:08.262
I'll now tell you the top five shadiest rumors about Mr. Furuse!

481
31:10.056 --> 31:13.267
In the Super Tech Expo planned in Konan City,

482
31:13.351 --> 31:15.061
the main sponsor, Isogai Tech,

483
31:15.144 --> 31:17.981
colluded with the police to commit technology theft.

484
31:18.064 --> 31:22.276
It is suspected that Mr. Furuse exerted pressure from behind the scenes.

485
31:23.027 --> 31:26.781
And then, Representative Furuse hatched a plan to get

486
31:26.864 --> 31:30.118
world-famous three-star chef Kohei Kajiwara

487
31:30.201 --> 31:34.163
to be the Expo's main food producer.

488
31:34.247 --> 31:39.127
However, there were complications, and the position remains vacant even now.

489
31:39.210 --> 31:41.671
Now, let's talk about the resort project,

490
31:41.754 --> 31:44.382
meant to take place in Konan City after the Expo.

491
31:44.465 --> 31:46.342
Its main contractor, Sendo,

492
31:46.426 --> 31:48.594
got involved in data fraud and embezzlement.

493
31:48.678 --> 31:53.808
It's suspected that some of the money was used by Mr. Furuse as his slush fund.

494
31:53.891 --> 31:57.854
Mr. Furuse seems to have used that money for lobbying activities

495
31:57.937 --> 32:00.982
to get supporters for the resort project.

496
32:01.065 --> 32:03.609
However, after the Sendo scandal,

497
32:03.693 --> 32:06.779
more and more politicians are opposing the resort project.

498
32:07.697 --> 32:09.323
Also, ten years ago,

499
32:09.407 --> 32:13.202
Mr. Furuse's secretary was assumed to have been murdered by an attorney.

500
32:13.286 --> 32:16.247
But now there's a possibility that she may be innocent.

501
32:16.330 --> 32:19.709
Mr. Furuse ordered a weekly tabloid to write articles

502
32:19.792 --> 32:22.336
slandering the attorney's reputation.

503
32:22.920 --> 32:27.216
And now, it's suspected he may even be involved in his secretary's murder.

504
32:32.263 --> 32:33.097
What is this?

505
32:33.181 --> 32:37.435
This is the reality of the resort plan that you are trying to invest in.

506
32:38.561 --> 32:42.398
The true nature of Furuse, whom you trust.

507
32:44.067 --> 32:45.985
I think you understand now.

508
32:47.153 --> 32:48.237
Mr. Murota!

509
32:50.281 --> 32:53.242
What is the meaning of this?

510
32:53.326 --> 32:55.078
No, well…

511
32:55.161 --> 32:58.456
You never told me any of this.

512
32:58.539 --> 33:00.166
This is basically a scam!

513
33:09.759 --> 33:11.469
METROPOLITAN POLICE

514
33:12.929 --> 33:14.305
We're the police.

515
33:22.188 --> 33:27.777
Mr. Kang, you must be careful when judging people.

516
33:34.951 --> 33:36.536
If what they said is correct,

517
33:37.245 --> 33:39.956
I'll need to have an investigation done in Korea.

518
33:40.623 --> 33:42.416
Please wait. I can explain--

519
33:42.500 --> 33:43.584
There's no need!

520
33:53.594 --> 33:54.428
This way.

521
34:06.649 --> 34:08.109
Let's hurry.

522
34:09.068 --> 34:11.112
-Hello. -Hello.

523
34:14.448 --> 34:16.242
I need a quick word with Mr. Furuse.

524
34:16.325 --> 34:18.619
Please check if he can step out of the meeting.

525
34:20.580 --> 34:21.914
Where did that man go?

526
34:21.998 --> 34:23.583
He went out from over there.

527
34:23.666 --> 34:25.668
-Go. -Yes, sir. Let's go.

528
34:26.294 --> 34:28.588
I'll go look for him too.

529
34:28.671 --> 34:29.839
Okay.

530
34:34.760 --> 34:36.846
-Split up and search! -Yes.

531
34:49.358 --> 34:50.651
We can't get out from here.

532
34:50.735 --> 34:52.862
What?! This wasn't in the plan!

533
34:52.945 --> 34:55.114
-Did we take the wrong route? -What do we do?

534
34:55.198 --> 34:56.949
Kureta. Sabayama.

535
34:57.033 --> 34:58.576
This way.

536
34:59.076 --> 35:00.161
Huh?

537
35:00.244 --> 35:01.454
Let's go!

538
35:09.253 --> 35:11.214
Are you sure this is the right way?

539
35:11.297 --> 35:13.549
I have the whole structure memorized.

540
35:14.133 --> 35:16.594
Mr. Uramawashi, please hurry up a bit.

541
35:16.677 --> 35:19.889
An architect shouldn't rush things.

542
35:19.972 --> 35:21.807
What is he even saying?

543
35:23.184 --> 35:25.019
Hey, wait…

544
35:25.561 --> 35:30.274
-Where is this? What is this place? -I don't know either.

545
35:32.151 --> 35:33.569
Let's check inside here.

546
35:33.653 --> 35:34.862
Yes!

547
35:36.739 --> 35:38.783
I have no idea where this is.

548
35:39.408 --> 35:41.327
I'm getting scared.

549
35:41.410 --> 35:42.745
It will be okay.

550
35:43.371 --> 35:45.331
Huh?

551
35:46.123 --> 35:47.291
Is that the exit?

552
35:48.000 --> 35:49.252
Over there?

553
36:08.187 --> 36:10.147
-First floor clear. -Head to the second.

554
36:10.231 --> 36:11.857
Search this floor!

555
36:11.941 --> 36:13.359
Are you serious?

556
36:13.442 --> 36:15.152
We need reinforcements downstairs!

557
36:15.236 --> 36:17.154
-Search down here. -Yes!

558
36:17.238 --> 36:19.115
It's possible he entered the boiler room.

559
36:19.198 --> 36:21.575
-Search this area. -Yes.

560
36:35.506 --> 36:38.467
There is no change to the blueprint.

561
36:38.551 --> 36:39.844
Blueprint?

562
36:41.262 --> 36:43.055
We're running away, right?

563
36:43.139 --> 36:44.015
Yeah.

564
36:52.231 --> 36:55.776
Did you see three strange men passing through here?

565
36:55.860 --> 36:57.445
Can't say I have.

566
36:57.528 --> 37:00.281
I see. Let's search elsewhere. Head back!

567
37:00.364 --> 37:01.532
Yes.

568
37:15.212 --> 37:17.006
Here they come.

569
37:22.345 --> 37:25.139
Hurry and get in. Hurry!

570
37:26.223 --> 37:27.224
Seatbelts!

571
37:27.308 --> 37:28.601
That was close.

572
37:28.684 --> 37:30.978
I didn't think Donghyuk would save us.

573
37:31.062 --> 37:33.522
-Won't the police raid our place? -Let's go home.

574
37:33.606 --> 37:34.774
Go!

575
37:41.822 --> 37:46.035
Uramawashi hasn't been found yet. He probably escaped.

576
37:46.118 --> 37:47.370
I see.

577
37:50.831 --> 37:53.751
I won't be meeting Mr. Furuse anymore.

578
37:54.293 --> 37:55.544
Understood?

579
38:18.192 --> 38:19.402
Huh?

580
38:19.485 --> 38:21.487
The evidence is all there,

581
38:21.570 --> 38:25.699
if you don't admit to the crime now, your sentence will only be longer.

582
38:26.283 --> 38:29.703
But I didn't kill Mr. Nitou.

583
38:29.787 --> 38:31.705
So why is there evidence?

584
38:31.789 --> 38:32.706
This is strange!

585
38:32.790 --> 38:33.958
Listen!

586
38:34.458 --> 38:36.544
You won't be able to see your son anymore.

587
38:39.713 --> 38:40.714
Taiji!

588
38:41.882 --> 38:43.259
Oh, it's Mom!

589
38:51.642 --> 38:53.519
You're late.

590
38:53.602 --> 38:55.271
Sorry I'm late.

591
38:55.354 --> 38:57.106
All right, let's go get some food.

592
38:57.189 --> 38:58.315
Yeah, I want ice cream.

593
38:58.399 --> 39:00.943
Really? Dessert already?

594
39:02.778 --> 39:04.738
Ms. Shiramoto, you have a visitor.

595
39:14.498 --> 39:19.003
Mr. Suzuhara told me what happened ten years ago.

596
39:20.212 --> 39:21.672
He apologized.

597
39:22.173 --> 39:24.967
He apologized for being fooled by the false articles.

598
39:25.050 --> 39:27.386
"Even though she was always so supportive," he said.

599
39:29.680 --> 39:31.390
And Mr. Moriki said

600
39:31.932 --> 39:36.103
that if you request a retrial, he'll lend a hand this time.

601
39:37.480 --> 39:39.607
I told you, I won't request a retrial.

602
39:40.107 --> 39:41.650
I did it.

603
39:42.526 --> 39:44.403
Please tell Mr. Moriki that too.

604
39:46.197 --> 39:47.781
I also met Taiji.

605
39:49.658 --> 39:50.868
Ten years ago,

606
39:51.368 --> 39:54.038
you didn't appeal because you worried about Taiji?

607
39:54.121 --> 39:55.581
Did you talk to him?

608
39:57.625 --> 39:59.418
What did you tell him?

609
40:00.252 --> 40:01.128
Ms. Shiramoto.

610
40:01.212 --> 40:03.172
Why did you have to do that?

611
40:03.255 --> 40:05.716
He has nothing to do with this. Don't involve him!

612
40:06.800 --> 40:08.636
I will protect Taiji.

613
40:09.553 --> 40:12.264
I won't let anything happen that would make you sad.

614
40:12.848 --> 40:17.269
I will stand beside you in court and fight for you. So--

615
40:17.353 --> 40:19.063
Leave me alone!

616
40:21.440 --> 40:22.483
Wait!

617
40:34.954 --> 40:36.330
Why…

618
40:38.999 --> 40:40.459
Not like this…

619
40:41.544 --> 40:43.546
I told her I wanted to meet you.

620
40:45.548 --> 40:47.591
Taiji knew everything.

621
40:52.638 --> 40:56.600
You're… my mom, right?

622
41:01.188 --> 41:03.023
I heard from Ms. Aso.

623
41:04.233 --> 41:08.070
Mom, you didn't actually do anything bad, right?

624
41:10.030 --> 41:11.365
Why?

625
41:11.448 --> 41:14.326
Why are you in prison when you didn't do anything wrong?

626
41:17.496 --> 41:19.790
You don't have to protect me.

627
41:19.873 --> 41:21.333
I'll be fine.

628
41:21.417 --> 41:23.419
I'm already a middle schooler!

629
41:24.753 --> 41:26.046
So…

630
41:38.350 --> 41:39.435
I'm sorry.

631
41:40.936 --> 41:41.937
Mom.

632
41:44.481 --> 41:46.275
I'm sorry, Taiji.

633
41:47.901 --> 41:49.111
I'm sorry.

634
41:51.572 --> 41:53.032
I'm so sorry.

635
41:54.575 --> 41:55.659
I'm sorry.

636
41:55.743 --> 41:58.537
I'm sorry. I'm truly so sorry.

637
42:04.501 --> 42:08.213
Ms. Shiramoto is now in favor of requesting a retrial.

638
42:11.383 --> 42:12.760
What did you do?

639
42:13.761 --> 42:17.348
I had Taiji meet Ms. Shiramoto and talk to her.

640
42:18.390 --> 42:21.226
So you are actually an uncle, Mr. Uramawashi.

641
42:21.310 --> 42:22.895
Was it Moriki?

642
42:23.854 --> 42:28.942
And so, after hearing Taiji's feelings, Ms. Shiramoto finally reconsidered--

643
42:29.026 --> 42:31.862
You used Taiji to play on her emotions.

644
42:33.781 --> 42:36.700
You also used quite a sneaky tactic.

645
42:36.784 --> 42:37.618
Sneaky?

646
42:37.701 --> 42:40.496
By doing that, she would have no choice but to agree!

647
42:40.579 --> 42:42.915
Please call it the power of love.

648
42:42.998 --> 42:46.418
Now we just need to organize the evidence for the retrial--

649
42:46.502 --> 42:48.379
Mr. Uramawashi. We have trouble.

650
42:49.296 --> 42:52.800
RGC Resorts Representative Kang Jun-ho…

651
42:52.883 --> 42:53.842
Look at that.

652
42:53.926 --> 42:56.303
Attended the three-day Japan-Korea Cultural Arts Forum

653
42:56.387 --> 42:59.848
and called for the necessity of economic cooperation.

654
42:59.932 --> 43:04.144
Furthermore, Mr. Furuse also attended this ceremony.

655
43:04.228 --> 43:09.983
After this event, I can truly feel that Mr. Kang and I share a strong bond.

656
43:10.067 --> 43:12.986
We showed Mr. Kang all that data yesterday, right?

657
43:13.070 --> 43:16.031
Didn't we create a rift between Furuse and Kang?

658
43:16.115 --> 43:19.702
-Why are they smiling and shaking hands? -What are you talking about?

659
43:19.785 --> 43:21.787
I thought we stopped their plan.

660
43:21.870 --> 43:23.539
But this is the result?

661
43:24.123 --> 43:25.708
We were deceived?

662
43:25.791 --> 43:29.044
So that's why the police didn't pursue us to our office.

663
43:31.463 --> 43:33.173
MR. MORIKI

664
43:34.925 --> 43:35.884
Yes?

665
43:35.968 --> 43:37.720
Is Uramawashi with you?

666
43:37.803 --> 43:39.388
Yes, he's right next to me.

667
43:42.266 --> 43:44.351
Uramawashi, can you hear me?

668
43:44.893 --> 43:46.353
I'm listening.

669
43:46.979 --> 43:52.067
Mr. Furuse just said he's going to sue you, Uramawashi.

670
43:52.151 --> 43:53.610
-What? -What?

671
43:53.694 --> 43:55.946
Come to my office right away!

672
43:56.530 --> 44:00.075
Mr. Furuse is suing you for defamation.

673
44:00.159 --> 44:05.456
He claimed you spread false news that greatly damaged his credibility.

674
44:05.539 --> 44:06.957
He is asking for

675
44:08.250 --> 44:09.418
300 million in damages.

676
44:09.501 --> 44:13.255
Isn't this a SLAPP lawsuit?

677
44:13.338 --> 44:15.632
So that's his move.

678
44:18.969 --> 44:20.888
What is a SLAPP lawsuit?

679
44:20.971 --> 44:22.639
It's a lawsuit claiming unreasonable damages,

680
44:22.723 --> 44:26.435
but whose real purpose is to silence people who criticize or protest.

681
44:26.518 --> 44:30.689
Big organizations or powerful individuals, guys like Furuse, have money.

682
44:30.773 --> 44:33.192
They can afford court costs and lawyer fees.

683
44:33.275 --> 44:35.444
But the person being sued can't do that.

684
44:35.527 --> 44:37.362
They'll be forced to stay quiet.

685
44:37.446 --> 44:39.239
That's absurd!

686
44:39.323 --> 44:41.950
Well, if we promise not to do anything further,

687
44:42.034 --> 44:44.411
there's a chance he would withdraw the lawsuit.

688
44:44.495 --> 44:46.830
Do you think Mr. Uramawashi would agree to that?

689
44:46.914 --> 44:48.332
Not a chance.

690
44:48.415 --> 44:51.710
Now that it has come to this, we have to fight.

691
45:01.011 --> 45:03.847
Today is also the day your business suspension ends.

692
45:06.266 --> 45:07.226
Sir…

693
45:14.942 --> 45:16.610
COURTHOUSE

694
45:21.532 --> 45:24.952
He's back to being a lawyer, but now he's the one getting sued.

695
45:25.035 --> 45:26.161
Typical Mr. Uramawashi.

696
45:26.245 --> 45:27.204
Yeah.

697
45:28.205 --> 45:29.331
All rise!

698
45:41.552 --> 45:43.804
This trial has only one purpose.

699
45:45.097 --> 45:49.268
Only after doubting everything does the truth become visible.

700
45:50.519 --> 45:51.937
That's a lie, right?

701
45:53.105 --> 45:56.275
This is the last piece.

702
45:56.358 --> 45:57.943
Your Honor,

703
45:58.026 --> 46:01.113
I'm submitting new evidence.

704
46:02.155 --> 46:03.115
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
